+# ArbiLend — Security Audit Report
+
+**Scope:** `src/LendingMarket.sol`, `src/CollateralVault.sol`, `src/PriceOracle.sol`,
+`src/MarketProxy.sol`, `src/interfaces/*` @ commit `aadaa46`.
+**Target:** Arbitrum One. **Status reviewed:** pre-deployment, no tests present.
+
+## Verdict
+
+**Do not deploy.** Six issues are individually fund-fatal on day one. Three of them
+(`upgradeTo`, `setOracle`, `setLiquidationThreshold`) are missing the `onlyOwner`
+modifier that every other privileged function in the same file has — any address can
+call them the block after deployment and take the entire market. The health factor
+formula is also numerically wrong in a way that liquidates well-collateralised users,
+and `borrowWithSig` has no replay protection.
+
+There is no test suite. Everything below is derived by reading the code; the fixes
+should land together with tests that reproduce each finding first.
+
+## Ranked summary
+
+| # | Sev | Contract · function | One line |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| C-1 | Critical | `LendingMarket.upgradeTo` | Anyone can replace the implementation and take every deposit |
+| C-2 | Critical | `LendingMarket.setOracle` | Anyone can swap in a fake oracle and drain the USDC float |
+| C-3 | Critical | `LendingMarket.healthFactor` | Division-before-multiplication: real LTV is 50%, users liquidated at 199% collateral |
+| C-4 | Critical | `LendingMarket.borrowWithSig` | No nonce/deadline — one signature is replayable forever |
+| C-5 | Critical | `LendingMarket.setLiquidationThreshold` | Anyone can freeze all collateral or mark every position liquidatable |
+| C-6 | Critical | `PriceOracle.getPrice` | No staleness / negative / round validation on the only price source |
+| H-1 | High | `LendingMarket.repay`, `_borrow`, `_liquidate`, `CollateralVault.*` | ERC-20 return values unchecked — USDT (next on the list) breaks or silently zeroes debt |
+| H-2 | High | `LendingMarket._borrow` | `borrow(0)` spam grows `borrowers` unboundedly, bricks `liquidateAll` permanently |
+| H-3 | High | `CollateralVault.withdraw` | Transfer before balance update — reentrancy drains the vault on any callback token |
+| H-4 | High | `PriceOracle.getPrice` | No Arbitrum sequencer-uptime check — mass wrongful liquidation on sequencer restart |
+| H-5 | High | Deployment config (README) | wstETH priced off the **stETH/USD** feed — collateral undervalued ~21% |
+| M-1 | Medium | `LendingMarket.initialize` | Implementation left uninitialised; proxy init front-runnable if `initData` is empty |
+| M-2 | Medium | `LendingMarket._liquidate` | No close factor — 100% of debt closed on a position 1 wei underwater |
+| M-3 | Medium | `LendingMarket._liquidate` | No bad-debt path — liquidator pays full debt for less-than-full collateral |
+| M-4 | Medium | `LendingMarket.liquidateAll` | Unbounded, all-or-nothing loop |
+| M-5 | Medium | `LendingMarket.listCollateral` | One global threshold, no per-asset LTV, no caps, no delisting |
+| M-6 | Medium | `CollateralVault.deposit` | Fee-on-transfer / rebasing tokens break accounting (both on the roadmap) |
+| M-7 | Medium | `LendingMarket.accrueInterest` | Interest derived from `block.number × 12` instead of `block.timestamp` |
+| M-8 | Medium | market-wide | No pause / emergency stop |
+| M-9 | Medium | `LendingMarket` | No way to withdraw treasury principal or interest |
+| M-10 | Medium | `LendingMarket` | Owner is immutable — no `transferOwnership`, no two-step handover |
+| L-1 | Low | `LendingMarket.repay` | Rounding dust means a position can never reach exactly zero debt |
+| L-2 | Low | `LendingMarket.accrueInterest` | Total interest depends on how often the permissionless accrue is called |
+| L-3 | Low | `LendingMarket.upgradeTo` | No codesize check — pointing at an EOA silently bricks the proxy |
+| L-4 | Low | `LendingMarket.initialize` | Domain separator cached; no zero-address validation |
+| L-5 | Low | `PriceOracle.getPrice` | Reverts for feeds with >18 decimals; `setFeed` unvalidated |
+| L-6 | Low | `MarketProxy` | Accepts ETH that nothing can ever move out |
