+
+## C-2 — `LendingMarket.setOracle` has no access control
+
+**Contract · function:** `src/LendingMarket.sol:91` — `setOracle(PriceOracle)`
+
+```solidity
+function setOracle(PriceOracle newOracle) external {   // <-- no onlyOwner
+    oracle = newOracle;
+```
+
+`setBorrowRate` and `listCollateral` directly below it both carry `onlyOwner`. This one
+and `setLiquidationThreshold` were missed.
+
+**What an attacker gets.** The oracle is the sole input to `collateralValueUsd` and
+`debtValueUsd`. Point it at a contract returning `1e30` for wstETH:
+
+1. Deposit 1 wei of wstETH.
+2. `setOracle(fakeOracle)`.
+3. `borrow(entire USDC balance of the market)` — the health check passes trivially.
+
+The treasury's whole seeded float leaves in one transaction. Alternatively, return a
+near-zero price for wstETH and liquidate every borrower for the 500 bps bonus, or
+return a huge price for USDC so every open position is instantly underwater.
+
+**Fix.** `external onlyOwner`. Additionally validate `address(newOracle) != address(0)`
+and consider a timelock on oracle rotation — swapping the price source is the single
+highest-impact governance action in the system and should not be instantaneous even
+for the real owner.
+
