+
+## M-6 — Fee-on-transfer and rebasing collateral break vault accounting
+
+**Contract · function:** `src/CollateralVault.sol:35-42` — `deposit(address,uint256)`
+
+```solidity
+IERC20(token).transferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount);
+balanceOf[msg.sender][token] += amount;   // credits the requested amount, not the received amount
+```
+
+**Impact.** For a fee-on-transfer token the vault credits more than it received; the
+last few users to withdraw find the vault short and their `transfer` reverts —
+first-out wins, last-out loses. For a **rebasing** token the problem is structural:
+`balanceOf` records absolute units, so a negative rebase leaves the vault under-funded
+and a positive rebase strands the yield in the contract with no owner. The README
+states the DAO has explicitly asked for "a path to yield-bearing and rebasing
+collateral," so this is a planned, not hypothetical, listing.
+
+**Fix.** Measure the delta rather than trusting the argument:
+
+```solidity
+uint256 before = IERC20(token).balanceOf(address(this));
+IERC20(token).safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount);
+uint256 received = IERC20(token).balanceOf(address(this)) - before;
+balanceOf[msg.sender][token] += received;
+```
+
+For rebasing tokens the delta pattern is necessary but not sufficient — switch to a
+share-based accounting model (`shares[user][token]` against `totalShares[token]` and the
+live contract balance) before listing any of them, or require the wrapped
+non-rebasing variant (wstETH over stETH) as a listing policy.
+
