+
+## M-8 — No pause or emergency stop
+
+**Contract · function:** market-wide — `src/LendingMarket.sol`, `src/CollateralVault.sol`
+
+There is no way to halt borrowing, liquidation, or deposits. The only lever governance
+holds is `upgradeTo`, which means the response to an oracle failure, a collateral-token
+compromise, or a sequencer incident is to write, review and ship a new implementation
+under time pressure.
+
+**Fix.** Add a `paused` flag with a `whenNotPaused` modifier on `borrow`,
+`borrowWithSig`, `CollateralVault.deposit`, and (separately gateable) `liquidate` —
+liquidation should usually keep running while borrowing is halted, but you want the
+ability to stop it during an oracle incident so you are not liquidating on bad prices.
+Never pause `repay` or `withdraw` for healthy users. A guardian role that can pause but
+not unpause is the usual split.
+
+---
+
+## M-9 — No path for the treasury to withdraw principal or interest
+
+**Contract · function:** `src/LendingMarket.sol` — no such function exists
+
+The README says "the treasury seeds the market's USDC balance with a direct transfer and
+takes the interest." There is no `withdrawReserves`, no `sweep`, no owner-controlled
+transfer of the debt asset. USDC enters via a raw transfer and via `repay`, and the only
+exit is `debtAsset.transfer(borrower, amount)` inside `_borrow`.
+
+**Impact.** All seeded capital and all accrued interest are locked in the proxy. Once
+C-1 is fixed, recovering them requires shipping an upgrade — which is a fund-recovery
+operation performed via the most dangerous function in the system. Also, nothing tracks
+how much of the balance is treasury principal versus accrued interest versus
+unborrowed float, so there is no on-chain notion of reserves at all.
+
+**Fix.** Add explicit accounting and a guarded exit:
+
+```solidity
+uint256 public totalReserves;   // append to storage layout
+
+function withdrawReserves(address to, uint256 amount) external onlyOwner {
+    if (amount > totalReserves) revert InsufficientReserves();
+    totalReserves -= amount;
+    debtAsset.safeTransfer(to, amount);
+}
+```
+
+Credit `totalReserves` from the interest portion in `accrueInterest`, and add a
+`totalBorrows` accumulator so utilisation is observable. This is also the foundation
+the v2 supply side will need.
+
+---
+
+## M-10 — Market ownership is immutable and single-key
+
+**Contract · function:** `src/LendingMarket.sol:18` — `owner`
+
+`owner` is set once in `initialize` and there is no `transferOwnership`. `PriceOracle`
+has one (single-step, but present); `LendingMarket` has none at all.
+
+**Impact.** If the deployer sets the wrong address, or the governance multisig needs to
+rotate, or the key is compromised, the only remedy is an upgrade — again routing a
+routine operation through the riskiest function in the system. Single-step transfer on
+`PriceOracle` also risks handing oracle control to a typo'd address, which under C-2's
+threat model is equivalent to handing over the market.
+
+**Fix.** Add two-step ownership (`transferOwnership` / `acceptOwnership`, i.e.
+OpenZeppelin `Ownable2Step`) to both `LendingMarket` and `PriceOracle`. Consider
+splitting `owner` into distinct roles — upgrader, risk-parameter setter, guardian —
+rather than one key that can do everything.
+
