+
+# Suggested order of work
+
+**Block the deploy on these (all six are one-transaction total-loss):**
+C-1, C-2, C-5 are a single ~10-minute change — add `onlyOwner` to three functions — and
+should go in immediately regardless of the rest of the schedule. C-3 is two lines. C-4
+and C-6 are each a contained rewrite of one function.
+
+**Then, before real money:** H-1 through H-5. H-5 is a config change but it is wrong
+*today* at 21% and needs the composed-feed work in `PriceOracle`, so start it early.
+H-1 and H-3 are prerequisites for the next listing round, not optional hardening.
+
+**Then:** the Medium set, prioritising M-1, M-8 and M-9 — those three determine whether
+you can respond to an incident at all. M-2/M-3 matter most once real leverage is on the
+book. M-5 and M-6 are prerequisites for listing weETH, ezETH, USDT or anything rebasing;
+do not start that listing round until they land.
+
+**Throughout:** L-7. Every fix above should arrive with a test that fails on `aadaa46`.
+
+## Notes on scope
+
+- This review is static. There are no tests to run and no deployment scripts in the
+  repository, so the deployment ordering (`CollateralVault`'s immutable `market` must be
+  the **proxy** address, not the implementation — if it is set to the implementation,
+  `seize` reverts and no position can ever be liquidated) could not be verified. Confirm
+  it before deploy.
+- Economic/parameter review (whether 8000 bps and a 500 bps bonus are correctly
+  calibrated for wstETH liquidity on Arbitrum, and whether 400 bps flat is viable
+  without a utilisation curve once v2 adds lenders) is out of scope here and worth a
+  separate pass.
+- `isCollateral` (`LendingMarket.sol:28`) is written by `listCollateral` and never read
+  anywhere. `CollateralVault.supported` is the actual gate. Dead state that can drift
+  from the real one — remove it or make it authoritative.

